[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked **known: one issue, one fix queued**. The reports merged
into it describe three different problems. Each problem has its own ticket.

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October: the parser fix shipped, and the booking-v3 form was
retired, so its hint will not be fixed. That ends two of the three problems. The third,
`one-day`, has no fix and its ticket stays open.

<Callout kind="warn">
A report of a booking that moved by one day is not #4471 and is not fixed. File it under
<a href="https://github.com/SimplifyAll/support-kb-4471/issues/3">#3</a>, not under the closed #4471.
</Callout>

## What is in #4471

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

The counts come from the data at render time. Each report is placed by its **tenant**: the
locale they write dates in and the booking form they run. Intake's tag is a guess from the
reporter's browser. Every report intake tagged `hint` came from an `en-US` browser, so the tag
says where the reporter sat, not what broke.

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant on file writes the day
first. A date like 6/5 (6 May) comes out as 5 June. Reports come from the app, email and the
booking-v2 forms of all eleven tenants. This is the bug #4471 names. **Fixed 5 Oct** (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`).

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form shows `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field.** People type month
first, as the hint tells them, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. Only
form reports from booking-v3 tenants fall here. The parser fix leaves this bug in place.
**Won't fix:** the booking-v3 form is retired, so no new reports can come from it.

**`one-day`: the booking moves by one day.** The month does not flip. The desk counts these reports under `parser`, where their tenant files them, so they show up in both rows. "Tuesday 6 October showed
as Monday." "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday." "Every booking in June
is one day off." The desk already noted these reports as a one-day move (desk-notes). The pattern
points at a time zone or daylight-saving conversion, not at date order. Neither the parser fix
nor retiring booking-v3 touches them. **Still open.**

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports with the same subject, and
the same few subjects ("Wrong day on the invite", "Date is wrong") cover all three problems.
Its consequences only mention the opposite case: one bug split across different subjects. They
don't cover one subject holding several bugs. When a big ticket's reports split by tenant,
channel or form, read the bodies before you mark it known.

